Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Code screens: no deadlock when a menu has its own slots;
 mod GUI sprites keep their nine-slice

- code_screens: code_screen_draw released the open screen's lock only at its end, but drawing the slots' frames
  asks where each slot is (code_screen_slot), which locks it again: a code screen of a menu with slots of its own
  (Mekanism's Teleporter) froze the game. The lock is now released before the frames.
- ui::load_metadata read gui.scaling only from minecraft's sprites: a content mod's sprite (<ns>:gui/sprites/...,
  as SPRITE draws them) was stretched whole instead of nine-sliced. It now reads every namespace's, keyed as the
  atlas names them; test a_content_mods_gui_sprites_keep_their_nine_slice_metadata.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
---
 crates/horizon-client-render/src/ui.rs        | 38 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../horizon-client/src/game/code_screens.rs   |  8 +++-
 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/horizon-client-render/src/ui.rs b/crates/horizon-client-render/src/ui.rs
index c1959c5a5..f955227e4 100644
